      "About ₹300!"
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "title": "Reading a Price List 📋",
   "text": "A price list shows the cost of many things. To buy several of one thing, MULTIPLY: 5 kg at ₹40 per kg = 5 × 40 = ₹200. To buy different things, add each amount.",
   "emoji": "📋",
   "bgColor": "from-blue-400 to-indigo-500",
   "spoken": "Multiply price per unit by how many, then add up different items.",
   "diagram": {
    "type": "generic-flow",
    "animate": true,
    "title": "Price list maths",
    "data": {
     "steps": [
      "1 kg = ₹40",
      "5 kg = 5 × 40",
      "= ₹200"
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "title": "Word Problems: Earn and Spend 💼",
   "text": "Money word problems tell a small story. A seller earns ₹250 on Monday and ₹350 on Tuesday. Together: 250 + 350 = ₹600. Read carefully — is it add or subtract?",
   "emoji": "💼",
   "bgColor": "from-emerald-400 to-teal-500",
   "spoken": "Earning and adding amounts together means addition; spending means subtraction.",
   "diagram": {
    "type": "generic-flow",
    "animate": true,
    "title": "Adding earnings",
    "data": {
     "steps": [
      "Earn ₹250",
      "Earn ₹350",
      "Total ₹600"
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "title": "Budgeting: Plan Your Money 📊",
   "text": "A BUDGET is a plan for money. Write what you NEED first — food, travel, school — and keep a little SAVED for later. A family with ₹2,000 plans: food ₹1,200, travel ₹500, savings ₹300!",
   "emoji": "📊",
   "bgColor": "from-purple-400 to-pink-500",
   "spoken": "A budget plans money for needs first, then saves the rest.",
   "diagram": {
    "type": "generic-flow",
    "animate": true,
    "title": "A simple budget",
    "data": {
     "steps": [
      "Budget ₹2,000",
      "Needs ₹1,700",
      "Save ₹300"
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "title": "Estimate to Check 💡",
   "text": "Round prices to check your maths! ₹198 is about ₹200, ₹121 is about ₹120. So ₹198 + ₹121 is about ₹320. If your exact answer is far from the estimate, check again!",
